WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.930
While Rika tried to figure out the whole Digivolution thing,

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:05.710
Calumon showed up to play, but Rika wasn't in the mood.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.810
Impmon appeared and tried to pick a fight with Renamon,

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:08.870
who wasn't in the mood either.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.950
Henry tried to teach Taccato that there's more to this taming business

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.770
than just flashing Modify cards.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.170
Then Rika was kidnapped by Ice Devimon,

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.270
who tried to make Rika his new tamer.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.270
The guys came to a rescue, but it was only when Rika admitted she needed her

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.550
that Renamon appeared.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.730
She Digivolved into Kyubimon and defrosted that icy dude.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.930
I think the whole experience kind of freaked Rika out.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.970
Why else would she say that she hate it all, did she?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.300
on

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:49.820
I hate Digimon.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.080
Modify!

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.760
All right, watch and learn, boys.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.420
I'm coming in for an aerial attack.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.110
Hyperwings!

00:01:58.830 --> 00:01:59.890
You're grounded, pal.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.140
Huh? That's it. I win.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.960
I can't believe you beat me.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.200
Amazing. What a game.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.440
I've never seen a combo like that before.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.840
Ha-ha. Not too shabby, huh?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.100
Hyrosphere!

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.760
I guess having real life experience kind of pays off, huh?

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:42.750
It's hardly even a challenge anymore playing the car game.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.730
What do you mean by real life experience?

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.190
Oh, too bad, but we seem to be out of time.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.850
Quit playing dumb, Chumlee.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:49.910
I heard what you said.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:50.990
Now what's up, huh?

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.750
You must be imagining things.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.450
Well, I gotta fly.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.070
It's been real.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.990
Come on, just one more game.

00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.170
Hey, get back here, goggle brain.

00:02:59.290 --> 00:02:59.970
I want a rematch.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.520
Sorry, buh-bye.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.930
No more.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.480
I'm sorry, but this is all that we have left right now.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.450
I'll bring you some fresh bread later with peanut butter, all right?

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.880
Mmm, okay.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.120
Good boy.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.800
We're a great team, aren't we, Gielmon?

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.920
There's not a Digimon around that's strong enough to beat the two of us.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:25.080
Yeah.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.910
People are giving me weird looks. You shouldn't have come.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.570
To Susie would have had me in tights in that tutu by now.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:40.690
It's embarrassing.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.220
Or some kind of strange fog over by the Westgate Bridge.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.020
Mind the weather changes fast here.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.210
Here they come.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:50.340
Digimon!

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.080
I can't seem to secure a tracer lock on the anomaly's data.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:06.740
We won't make it in time. It's going to bio-emerge.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.540
Use UGoth. Stop that thing.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.950
It's too late, sir. It's already begun.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.010
Full breach estimated in 60 seconds.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:16.490
At this point, the application of the UGoth program could be extremely dangerous.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:20.290
Don't question me. Circumvent the safety grid and release the program now.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.370
That wild one is a ticking time bomb.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:23.150
Apply.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.210
how nice the view is from up here,

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.210
but how long do you think it'll stay this way

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.270
if we don't check it out?

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.940
Hey, Terrier Mon, wait!

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.440
Come on, hen!

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.020
Gotcha!

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.160
Hey, that hurt!

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:47.720
We've got to go home now.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.500
We're going home.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:50.520
Wait a minute.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.140
Please don't tell me you changed your mind

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.240
about Susie and the tutu.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:54.300
Do it!

00:04:58.860 --> 00:04:59.960
Terrier Mon, how many...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:07.950
times do I have to tell you stop why don't we let someone else handle this

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:13.320
for a change confirmed you got this found the wild one make sure it's

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.460
completely destroyed I want nothing left

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:39.980
That's someone else handling it.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.450
Termination of Wild One is confirmed.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.870
Tally, get me an analysis of the impact on the real world right away.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.510
Plus all the data you've got on the point of termination.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.040
No matter how they play at being living creatures,

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.640
they're nothing more than just trash on the internet to me.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:56.560
Fire.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:08.850
I've never explained why you wouldn't let me fight before.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:10.090
What's up with that?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.450
Nothing's up. I just don't want you to fight, okay?

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:16.440
Rico was right. You are starting to sound like a broken record.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:20.280
Leave her out of this. It's just that on the net, Digimon only exists to do battle.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.800
So because I'm here now, you want me to lay around like a house. Is that right?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.920
Are you going to let me explain or not?

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:33.220
Henry, you once told me that my very existence in the real world was wrong.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.760
Is that still true? Is that how you feel about me?

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:41.070
Because if it is, I'll sign up for the Miss Pretty Fans treatment right now.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.140
You just say the word.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.780
Hey, you know that's not what I meant. We're a team.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:55.030
Never explained why you wouldn't let me fight before.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:56.560
What's up with that?

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:03.900
Nothing's up. I just don't want you to fight, okay?

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:08.700
I have to fight sometime, but when?

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:16.510
Huh?

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:40.150
I'm gonna get some more milk, okay? I'll be right back.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.210
Do it.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.360
I'm out of here.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.630
She wants me to follow her.

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:07.080
Bitch me if you can.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.100
I said I didn't make any friends yesterday.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:15.850
Hate them.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:16.150
Huh?

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:18.610
I hate Digimon, all of them!

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:19.390
Huh?

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.180
Them anyway.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:29.920
Random?

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:34.320
Nope, throw this away, huh?

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.350
Get out of my room, you overgrown rat.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.440
You're not happy, are you?

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.820
Play, you happy?

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:43.640
Oh, please.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:49.740
Later, this'll make you...

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:57.190
Well?

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:11.100
For some reason, Terriormon feels like he has to fight.

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:14.310
Why would I purposely put my friend in danger?

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:19.210
Just doesn't understand that if anything ever happened to him because of me,

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:21.730
never forgive myself.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:35.680
Until recently, I thought my only purpose here in the real world was to fight and load the data of those I defeated.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:40.480
Digivolving and vanquishing my enemies were the only things that made me feel worthy.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:45.340
And Rika, her only attachment to me was as a tamer who could make me stronger.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.160
But now I'm not so sure.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:53.440
There's gotta be a bigger reason why me and my friends were chosen to be Digimon tamers in the first place.

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:58.650
It would help both of us if we could just figure that out.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:09:59.980
What are you...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.420
What do you think?

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:02.160
Renamon.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:03.120
Hello?

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:16.650
For our luck, you don't have cheese to sleep.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:46.010
Hey, what are you doing out here?

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:47.650
Have you taken up birdwatching or something?

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.850
I was hoping another Digimon would show up.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.420
I'm ready for another battle.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:52.410
Huh?

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:54.930
I want to use that combination on Geomon again.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.260
I think you need a vacation, huh?

00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:58.820
There you are.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:10:59.940
Thought you could escape.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:00.550
Huh?

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:00.970
Huh?

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:02.810
What do you want?

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:07.050
Revenge, Takatoad, for that stupid combination you pulled on me yesterday.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:08.250
I want a rematch.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:10.530
Yeah, apparently you think you're hot stuff now.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.330
Think you can take us again, big shot?

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.090
You sound pretty tough from way over there, huh?

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:18.130
I'll take you both on any time with whatever you've got.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:19.600
I'm ready now.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:21.600
Say your prayers, cause you're going down.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:22.480
Let's go!

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:27.700
Hey, don't you boys ever get tired of Digimon?

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:28.940
That's all you talk about.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:29.980
Oh, you

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.870
You know, Jerry, kids will be kids.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:35.810
Maybe we are just kids, but at least we have a hobby.

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:36.510
Now scram!

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:44.230
Mickey, we have more important things to do.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:45.350
That's silly, boys.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:48.050
Girls, I don't think I'll ever understand them.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.730
Well, Chumlee, you ready?

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:50.610
Sure, yeah.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.130
Hey, Henry, are you coming along too?

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:54.420
Where'd he go?

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:57.080
Are we going shopping?

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:58.260
We're doing nothing.

00:11:58.460 --> 00:11:59.780
You were supposed to stay home, remember?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.240
Or go home after what she did.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:06.140
Susie's Chamber of Horrors is worse than battling any Digimon.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:08.040
Come on.

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:10.780
Patience, Grasshopper.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:11.940
Guess what?

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.660
I won, Mr. Invincible!

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.520
I can't believe I didn't see that coming.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.300
I hope you enjoyed your little victory yesterday,

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.620
because you'll never have one again.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.560
Yeah, all you're gonna feel is pain when we keep whooping you.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.080
Well, it's just a stupid car game anyway.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.760
I have much more important things to do with my time.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.630
Winning a real Digimon battle is what separates the boys from the men.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:34.860
Real Digimon?

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.420
Who you trying to kid here, pal?

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.180
You're a loser and a liar.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.320
Yeah, I am not.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.100
Yeah, and I've got the Loch Ness Monster in my bathtub.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:43.860
You want to see him?

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:45.040
Show me a real Digimon.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:45.800
I will.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:46.600
Give it up.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:47.920
I'm not lying.

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:49.600
Okay, then prove it.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:50.080
Well?

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:51.260
Hey, come on.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.140
Nessie's waiting.

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:53.240
All right.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.960
You ask for it and you're going to get it.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:55.720
Follow me.

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:57.550
All right.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:12:59.960
Now you got to...

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:01.680
I swear that you won't tell anyone about this.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:02.380
Whatever.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:03.220
I swear.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:06.060
Gilmon?

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.190
Yeah right, doofus.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.310
You're so full of it.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.220
So, did you call me?

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:32.560
Yeah, were you asleep?

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.200
Well, it was my nappy time.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:39.320
Sorry, I didn't bring any bread with me this time.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.220
I don't care about that.

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:44.430
Smell a Digimon.

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:45.110
Yeah!

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.960
It's yours locked, and Yugoth has been-

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.540
Say goodbye.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:13.970
What was that?

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.470
The Wild one we terminated earlier just completely destroyed Yuga.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:29.440
I need to know where he is now.

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.980
We've lost him. He's just bio-emerged.

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.340
Somebody needs a tune-up.

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:46.770
What's going on?

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:09.800
Oh, it's the Samurai Master Musiyamon, a champion-level wizard type.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:13.080
He can slice and dice an entire city with his Shogun sword.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.470
This is mine!

00:15:58.960 --> 00:15:59.980
Now you can do it.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:03.860
Looks like we've got company, Henry.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.680
Don't even think about it.

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:08.510
I've confirmed the bio-emergence point coordinates

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:11.170
at the west intersection of the Shinjuku Big Guard cable.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:12.530
Excellent.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.300
The fog's so thick, I can't see the signal.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:18.420
Come on, Henry.

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:19.700
Aren't you curious?

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:32.650
Why did you fly away?

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:36.080
Fight me, you human coward!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:38.250
This is bad!

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.540
Demodify for wings!

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:49.440
Something doesn't feel right.

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.380
Use the wings like last time.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.840
You could do it. I tried.

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:56.460
I can't stop!

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.200
Is that the best you've got?

00:16:58.400 --> 00:16:59.700
Takato, watch out!

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.740
What now? If I do nothing, we'll all be made into sushi.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:13.460
I don't think I can talk us out of this one.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:21.300
Gotta stop him.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:22.560
Well, it's about time.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:38.490
Hyper Sonic, activate!

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:42.570
Time to teach this bad boy it's not safe to play with LIFE!

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:48.740
Finish the job!

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:49.920
Okay!

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:54.530
This will help!

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:56.540
Ditching the pollution!

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:34.340
Gunsword!

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:43.560
I'll save you.

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:44.690
Yay!

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:52.000
Ciao, Gargoman.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:56.260
Go.

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:56.820
What?

00:18:57.630 --> 00:18:58.010
Thank you.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:07.690
Let's go.

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:12.630
Let's get her back before anyone notices.

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:20.310
Can you see that?

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:25.600
Oh, yeah, they're beautiful.

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:26.700
Come on now, let's go.

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:36.760
Yeah, there really was no other choice.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.400
I guess Terriormon was right.

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:39.800
Sometimes you have to fight.

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:41.540
Goodbye, human!

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:44.800
Terriormon, I mean Gargamon, I owe you an apology.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:46.920
There are some battles worth fighting.

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:47.450
Yep.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:49.380
Now that we're working together as partners,

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.480
I guess I need to learn more about taming.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:53.170
Momentum.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.980
Hey, Gilmon, I owe you an apology, too.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:58.260
I really messed up today.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:19:59.980
I just kept swiping...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:03.440
One card after another, I didn't even think about what might happen to you.

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:06.650
No problem. I kind of like flying anyway.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:08.720
Tell me mine.

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:10.520
Momentai?

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:10.960
Hmm?

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:12.620
Momentai.

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:14.920
Momentai!

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:16.940
Momentai?

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.980
No, Gilman, it's Momentai!

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:25.330
Is Hypnos lost control?

00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:27.770
How can these guys Momentai at a time like this?

